  "checks": [
    "Rotation runs after creation, hourly and through manual retention. It keeps the configured newest archives plus the latest complete archive and temporarily protects a newly created archive. Deletion is bounded to 64 per pass.",
    "Quarantined removals recover before policy evaluation; unknown files, symbolic links, hard-linked files and wrong format headers are not candidates. Deferred cleanup is reported.",
    "Backup retention can be edited with bounded numeric controls; changing the count preserves key and source settings.",
    "Exports use one pinned state/file snapshot, 51 explicitly reviewed JSON Lines tables, original file bodies and a SHA-256 manifest. A changed or new schema requires an explicit export-policy update.",
    "Authentication tables, key material, protected calendar links, HTTP validators, provider endpoints and raw state.db are excluded. Partial file sets produce an explicitly partial archive and CLI exit 4.",
    "Export files use numeric directories and escaped names; original locations remain in the manifest. Backslashes, reserved names, trailing dots, case differences and long names cannot create unsafe or colliding archive paths.",
    "Backup/export reads reject links in every root ancestor, closing a parent-directory redirection gap. Descriptor-based reads still reject linked file entries.",
    "CLI streaming requires recent-password confirmation, validates length, preserves existing destinations, uses private output files and closes its temporary session. Server temporary export files are removed when the response stream closes.",
    "Expected OpenAPI additions were reviewed: two export operations, two retention schemas and additive retention/settings properties. The composition addition is one shared export port."
  ],
